  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Aviation Sustainability &quot;Green Routes&quot; Initiative FAA Transfer Funds, through U.S. Government - Department of Transportation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA funding is enabling the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration to deliver training and program support for the USTDA-funded U.S.-China Aviation Cooperation Program Civil Aviation Sustainability &quot;Green Routes&quot; Initiative Technical Assistance (TA). The TA is envisioned to be the first of three phases under the Green Routes Pilot Program (GRPP), which aims to continue U.S.-China joint aviation-related energy conservation and emission reduction collaboration. The GRPP is intended to strengthen the efficiency and safety of China&apos;s aviation system, while assisting U.S. companies gain market entry into the Chinese aviation sector.</narrative>
  </description>
